      "summary": {
        "text": "Rinat Salikhov (Russian: Ринат Салихов; born 15 December 1985) is a Russian racing driver who last competed for Winward Racing in GT World Challenge Europe.\n\nBetween 2014 and 2019, Salikhov competed in the Blancpain Endurance Series for Ferrari and Rinaldi Racing, achieving an overall podium finish at Monza and a class victory at the 24 Hours of Spa. In 2019, he won the Gulf 12 Hours overall for Attempto Racing. Salikhov returned to GT World Challenge Europe in 2025, driving a Mercedes-AMG for Winward Racing.",
        "lang": "en",
        "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rinat_Salikhov"
      },
